/*!
\example TCP_Server.cpp
This is an example for a very simple TCP server application.
It waits for a clients, sends a fixed message and disconnect again.
When nobody connects within 5s, the server shuts down.

\b Output when the TCP_Client is started:
\verbatim
Waiting for a client...
Client connected from 127.0.0.1:35296
Successfully sent 43 bytes.
Waiting for a client...
Timed out waiting for a client.
\endverbatim
*/

/*!
\example TCP_Client.cpp
This is an example for a very simple TCP client application.
IT connects to a server, blocking until connected and reads available data until the read times out.

\b Output when the TCP_Server example is running:
\verbatim
Using server: 127.0.0.1
Received data from server: The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog
\endverbatim
*/

/*!
\example TCP_Client_Reconnect.cpp
A more advanced TCP client exmaple with reconection logic and full error handling.
Demonstrates usability of real-world reconnect logic without an separate even loop.

\b Output when the TCP_Server example is running:
\verbatim
Connect failed
Connected to 127.0.0.1:47777
Received data from server: The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog
Server disconnected; reconnecting
\endverbatim
*/

/*!
\example UDP_Multicast.cpp
This is a simple example on how to do UDP multicast sending and receiving.

\b Output if any local network is available:
\verbatim
Received from 192.168.178.15:46734: Welcome to our multicast group!
\endverbatim
*/

/*!
\example UDP_Commands.cpp
UDP server and client in blocking mode, sending commands from console.

\b Output when commands are sent via console agruments:
\verbatim
Listening for UDP commands on 127.0.0.1:47778
Received from 127.0.0.1:52659 test
Received from 127.0.0.1:35080 quit
Stopping.
\endverbatim
*/

/*!
\example mini_ifconfig.cpp
Very basic network configuration using the libraries built-in functions.

\b Output without arguments lists all interfaces:
\verbatim
lo:
        mtu 65536
        inet 127.0.0.1 netmask 255.0.0.0 broadcast 0.0.0.0
        ether
enp12s0:
        mtu 1500
        inet 192.168.178.15 netmask 255.255.255.0 broadcast 192.168.178.255
        ether 30:c5:99:5b:ea:63
\endverbatim
*/


/*!
\example EventHandler_Timer.cpp
Demonstrates the use of different timers and basic use the the EventHAndler class.
*/

/*!
\example UDP_Event_Receiver.cpp
Shows how independent UDP receivers are dispatched by one event loop in a single thread.
*/

/*!
\example TCP_Event_Server.cpp
A full non-blocking TCP server handling multiple clients in a signle tread.
*/
